model g6_refusal_keys_typed
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.6 (#57, P4), G6: which refusal a place keeps (E §4.1): one plan move m of two keys, a place and a flat of a list index, with two instances on one day, m[x, f3] and m[x, f11], each a leg into gone after its lifespan ends (RUN-LIFESPAN), both refused at src. Of a day's legs refused at one place the first in the typed movement order prints: f3 (position 3) before f11 (position 11), so bal(src) prints m[x, f3].cash, where the order's text (f11 before f3) printed m[x, f11].cash. Its twin makes m[x, f3] a leg of 0, so m[x, f11].cash refuses alone."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

index flats = [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8, f9, f10, f11]

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

place x: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

move m[p in accounts on d0, f in flats]: transfers
  on d0
  when p == x and (pos(f) == 3 or pos(f) == 11)
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[x] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
